Alkyl halides are hydrolysed to corresponding alcohols by boiling with aqueous alkali solution ( $\mathrm{NaOH}$ or $\mathrm{KOH}$ ).

\mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CH}_{2} \mathrm{I}+\mathrm{KOH} \longrightarrow \mathrm{CH}_{3} \mathrm{CH}_{2} \mathrm{OH}+\mathrm{KI}

This is nucleophilic substitution reaction in which the attacking nucleophile is $\mathrm{OH}^{-}$.

Wurtz reaction for the preparation of ethane is

\underset{1}{\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{I}+2 \mathrm{Na}}+\underset{\mathrm{ICH}}{\mathrm{ICH}_3} \stackrel{\text { dry ether }}{\longrightarrow} \underset{1 \mathrm{~mole}}{\mathrm{C}_2 \mathrm{H}_6}+2 \mathrm{NaI}

$1 \mathrm{~mole} \quad 1 \mathrm{~mole} \quad 1 \mathrm{~mole}$
Number of moles of $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{I}$ required for the manufacture of 1 mole _2 \mathrm{H}_6=2$ moles
Weight of 2 moles of $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{I}$
\begin{aligned}
& =2 \times(12+3+127) \\
& =2 \times(142) \\
& =284 \mathrm{~g}
\end{aligned}

\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{PhCH}_2 \mathrm{Cl} \stackrel{\text { aq. } \mathrm{NaCN}}{\longrightarrow} \mathrm{PhCH}_2 \mathrm{CN} \\
& \stackrel{\text { Cat. hydrogenation }}{\stackrel{\mathrm{H}_2, \mathrm{Pd}}{\longrightarrow}} \mathrm{PhCH}_2 \mathrm{CH}_2 \mathrm{NH}_2
\end{aligned}

